<%- include('partials/head', { title, apiBase, active }) %>

<h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Database</h1>
<p class="mt-1 max-w-2xl text-sm text-gray-600">
  Connect your own PostgreSQL database and pull its tables straight into
  <code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5">data/raw/connectors/postgres/</code> as knowledge -- from there they flow
  through the normal compiler pipeline (extraction, synthesis, linking) exactly like any other raw source. Credentials
  are encrypted at rest and only the row counts/column names you choose to import ever leave your database.
</p>

<div id="sample-db-callout" class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-indigo-100 bg-indigo-50 p-4 text-sm text-indigo-900">
  <p class="font-semibold">Don't have a Postgres database handy?</p>
  <p class="mt-1 text-indigo-800">
    <code class="rounded bg-white px-1 py-0.5">docker compose up</code> also starts a small seeded PostgreSQL
    container (service <code class="rounded bg-white px-1 py-0.5">postgres</code>) with a sample Aurora Labs
    knowledge base -- departments, employees, projects, and KB articles -- so you can try the whole flow end to end
    without any data of your own. See <code class="rounded bg-white px-1 py-0.5">docker/postgres/init.sql</code> and
    <code class="rounded bg-white px-1 py-0.5">documentation/39-postgres-database-connector.md</code>.
  </p>
  <button type="button" id="use-sample-values-btn" class="mt-3 rounded-lg bg-indigo-900 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-white hover:bg-indigo-800">
    Fill the form with the sample database's values
  </button>
  <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-indigo-700">
    Pre-fills host <code class="rounded bg-white px-1 py-0.5">postgres</code> (the Compose service name), which is
    correct when this app is also running via <code class="rounded bg-white px-1 py-0.5">docker compose up</code>.
    Running the backend outside Docker instead? Change the host to <code class="rounded bg-white px-1 py-0.5">localhost</code>
    -- the container still publishes port 5432 to the host.
  </p>
</div>

<section class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-card">
  <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Connect a database</h2>
  <form id="connect-form" class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
    <label class="flex flex-col gap-1 text-xs font-medium text-gray-600">Label
      <input name="account_label" type="text" required placeholder="my-database" class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-2 py-1.5 text-sm" />
    </label>
    <label class="flex flex-col gap-1 text-xs font-medium text-gray-600">Host
      <input name="host" type="text" required placeholder="localhost" class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-2 py-1.5 text-sm" />
    </label>
    <label class="flex flex-col gap-1 text-xs font-medium text-gray-600">Port
      <input name="port" type="number" value="5432" class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-2 py-1.5 text-sm" />
    </label>
    <label class="flex flex-col gap-1 text-xs font-medium text-gray-600">Database
      <input name="dbname" type="text" required placeholder="aurora_kb" class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-2 py-1.5 text-sm" />
    </label>
    <label class="flex flex-col gap-1 text-xs font-medium text-gray-600">User
      <input name="user" type="text" required placeholder="wiki_reader" class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-2 py-1.5 text-sm" />
    </label>
    <label class="flex flex-col gap-1 text-xs font-medium text-gray-600">Schema
      <input name="schema" type="text" value="public" class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-2 py-1.5 text-sm" />
    </label>
    <label class="flex flex-col gap-1 text-xs font-medium text-gray-600">Password
      <input name="password" type="password" required class="rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-2 py-1.5 text-sm" />
    </label>
    <div class="flex items-end">
      <button type="submit" class="rounded-lg bg-gray-900 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:bg-gray-800">Connect</button>
    </div>
  </form>
  <p id="connect-error" class="mt-2 hidden text-xs text-red-600"></p>
</section>

<section class="mt-6">
  <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Connected databases</h2>
  <div id="accounts-list" class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-4"></div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/foot', { clientScript }) %>
